data post_cutover_race_repair_note: String = "Repair row block (2026-08-01): these eleven paths (eight CI-heal/workflow paths, three source-integration proof-kernel paths from PR 7563) merged to main from branches cut BEFORE the placement gate landed (#7560), so main itself carried post-cutover Added paths with no publication decision and the gate refused every subsequent PR merge ref. Each is public CI/heal/workflow machinery; Publish World is the deliberate decision for all eleven. The race class dissolves when the placement gate becomes a required branch-protection check: a merge ref must then stamp its own added files before merging, so main can never re-enter this state."

data roster_duplicate_repair_note: String = "THE REPAIR ABOVE WAS APPLIED TWICE AND THE SECOND COPY WAS A REFUSAL, not spare bytes. Three sessions reached the same red main independently and each wrote the same eleven rows: #7565 sorted them into the list, #7580 appended them again as a block, and this branch had authored its own copy before either landed. Both landed copies reached main, so main carried each of the eleven paths twice. That is not benign duplication -- the gate reads the roster it is handed, and repeats are exactly what it refuses: file_marker_audit emits FilePublishGrantMarkerRepeated per repeated path, and public_file_grant_lookup answers PublicFileGrantAmbiguous, which becomes AddedPathPublishGrantAmbiguous for every one of them. A roster that grants a path twice cannot say which grant authorized it, so the gate declines to guess (DESIGN section 5: refuse, never widen). The repair for a red main therefore re-redded it by a second cause, and the merge resolving this branch keeps one row per path rather than the union of both spellings.\\n\\nWHY THIS RECURS AND WHAT ACTUALLY DISSOLVES IT: a defect on main blocks every lane at once, so every lane discovers it simultaneously and fixes it locally, and the fixes then collide. Deduplicating by hand each time is the same work re-paid per collision. The structural end is the trigger post_cutover_race_repair_note already names -- the placement gate as a required branch-protection check, so a merge ref stamps its own added paths and no backfill is ever needed -- plus set semantics for this roster, since a list keyed by path is a Map wearing a List's clothes and duplicate keys are unwritable in the former."

data public_publication_grant_roster: PublicPublicationGrantRoster = PublicPublicationGrantRoster {
  baseline: public_root_publish_baseline,
  file_grants: public_file_publish_grants,
}
